<com:TContent ID="body">

<h1>THiddenField Sample</h1>

<com:THiddenField ID="Hidden1" Value="alpha" OnValueChanged="valueChanged" />

<table class="sampletable">

<tr><td class="samplenote">
Read the hidden field on the server:
</td><td class="sampleaction">
<com:TButton Text="Read the value" OnClick="readValue" />
</td></tr>

<tr><td class="samplenote">
Write a new value from the server. The new value reaches the browser with the next page:
</td><td class="sampleaction">
<com:TButton Text="Write a new value" OnClick="writeValue" />
</td></tr>

<tr><td class="samplenote">
Write a value on the client, then post the form. The value survives the round trip and
raises <tt>OnValueChanged</tt>:
</td><td class="sampleaction">
<input type="button" value="Set the value to 'set by the browser'"
	onclick="document.getElementById('<%= $this->Hidden1->ClientID %>').value = 'set by the browser';" />
</td></tr>

<tr><td class="samplenote">
Server-side value:
</td><td class="sampleaction">
<com:TLabel ID="Result" Text="Nothing has been read yet." />
</td></tr>

<tr><td class="samplenote">
The <tt>OnValueChanged</tt> event fires when the posted value differs from the previous
one:
</td><td class="sampleaction">
<com:TLabel ID="ChangeLog" Text="The value has not changed yet." />
</td></tr>

</table>

</com:TContent>
